Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:00:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: report the T6031 GPU to the PMP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The T6031 (M3 Max) G15 GPU is powered by its PMGR domain alone, with no
RTKit vote, and nothing sets its PTD power request. PMP then ignores the
GPU's bandwidth demand and memory stays at its idle floor.

Port the T6030 report (9bb74767dc) to T6031: AGX is the acknowledged
soc-device ID 14 (record 13) of the J516C table, on the T6031 report
apertures. Set it after firmware and backend setup, clearing it first,
since an earlier request is acknowledged without enabling bandwidth
scaling. A failure only warns and clears the request, which is how the
GPU ran before. The session and the request stay until reboot.

With Mesa unchanged, compute-copy bandwidth (test-backend-ops perf -o CPY,
Vulkan) goes from 75 to 316 GB/s for 1.5 GB f32 copies and from 56 to
200 GB/s for 768 MB f16/bf16 copies. Tested on an M3 Max J516C, on top
of local patches (HDMI, panel brightness, AVD AV1, in-flight cap); the
panel, HDMI, brightness and AVD keep working.

